content:
Project Overview
A website (index.html + style.css) being optimized for mobile responsiveness. All major sections have been fixed for mobile layout, and image sharpness/rendering has been improved globally and per-component.

## Completed Work
1. Fixed navbar mobile layout (hamburger + logo centering)
2. Fixed hero section mobile layout (text, image, padding)
3. Fixed stats strip mobile (2-col grid, spacing)
4. Fixed about section mobile (single column, badge positioning)
5. Fixed products grid mobile (2-col → 1-col on small screens)
6. Fixed why-us grid mobile (2-col → 1-col)
7. Fixed gallery grid mobile (2-col, proper sizing)
8. Fixed testimonials mobile (single column)
9. Fixed contact section mobile (single column, form padding)
10. Fixed footer mobile (single column, spacing)
11. Fixed general overflow/horizontal scroll issues
12. Fixed gallery image rendering on mobile (768px): changed from fixed height to `height: auto; width: 100%; max-height: 150px; object-fit: contain` with crisp-edges rendering
13. Added global mobile image sharpness rule inside `@media (max-width: 768px)`: `image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast; image-rendering: crisp-edges; -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden; backface-visibility: hidden; transform: translateZ(0)`
14. Fixed about section image rendering on mobile: added `image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast; image-rendering: crisp-edges` to `.about-img-main` and `.about-img-badge`
15. Fixed product images at 480px breakpoint: changed from fixed `height: 120px` to `height: auto; width: 100%; max-height: 140px; object-fit: contain` with crisp-edges rendering; also reduced `min-height` of `.product-img-wrap` to 140px
16. Fixed gallery images at 480px breakpoint: changed from fixed `height: 110px` to `height: auto; width: 100%; max-height: 120px; object-fit: contain` with crisp-edges rendering

## Key Technical Decisions
- Mobile breakpoint: `@media (max-width: 768px)`
- Secondary breakpoint: `@media (max-width: 480px)`
- Gallery images use `object-fit: contain` with `max-height: 150px` (768px) / `max-height: 120px` (480px) instead of fixed height
- Product images use `object-fit: contain` with `max-height: 140px` at 480px breakpoint
- Global `img` rule inside mobile media query uses GPU-accelerated rendering (`transform: translateZ(0)`) and backface-visibility hidden to improve sharpness
- `image-rendering: crisp-edges` applied globally on mobile and specifically to about/gallery/product images at both breakpoints

## Relevant Files & Code
- `index.html` — Main HTML structure (open in VSCode, not directly modified in recent steps)
- `style.css` — All styles; mobile fixes are in `@media (max-width: 768px)` block starting around line 1236; 480px fixes around line 1330+

Key CSS snippets added/modified:
```css
/* Inside @media (max-width: 768px) */
img {
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
  -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  transform: translateZ(0);
}

.gallery-item img {
  height: auto;
  width: 100%;
  max-height: 150px;
  object-fit: contain;
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
}

.about-img-main {
  max-height: 200px;
  padding: 10px;
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
}

.about-img-badge {
  width: 72px; height: 72px;
  bottom: -8px; right: -8px;
  padding: 8px;
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
}

/* Inside @media (max-width: 480px) */
.product-img-wrap { min-height: 140px; padding: 10px 8px; }
.product-img-wrap img {
  height: auto;
  width: 100%;
  max-height: 140px;
  object-fit: contain;
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
}

.gallery-item img {
  height: auto;
  width: 100%;
  max-height: 120px;
  object-fit: contain;
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  image-rendering: crisp-edges;
}
```

## Current Status
All mobile layout tasks are completed. Most recent work: applied consistent `height: auto / max-height / object-fit: contain / crisp-edges` image rendering fixes to both product and gallery images at the 480px breakpoint, matching the approach already used at the 768px breakpoint.

## Pending Tasks
None — all requested tasks have been completed.
